## 2. `packages/core/src/idea/ops/store.ts` — File storage patterns

`/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/packages/core/src/idea/ops/store.ts`

This is the most relevant example because it uses JSON for metadata and markdown+frontmatter for content. There is NO yaml-js usage here — it uses `gray-matter` for frontmatter parsing. Key patterns:

**Read JSON:**
```ts
const content = readFileSync(jsonPath, "utf-8");
const raw = JSON.parse(content) as RawIdeaSession;
```

**Write JSON:**
```ts
writeFileSync(jsonPath, JSON.stringify(session, null, 2), "utf-8");
```

**Read YAML frontmatter (markdown files):**
```ts
import matter from "gray-matter";

function parseFrontmatter(content: string) {
  const parsed = matter(content);
  return { frontmatter: parsed.data, body: parsed.content };
}
```

**Write YAML frontmatter manually (no yaml serializer, just string templates):**
```ts
const frontmatterLines = [
  "---",
  `name: ${input.name}`,
  `description: ${input.description}`,
  "---",
];
const content = frontmatterLines.join("\n") + "\n\n" + promptContent;
writeFileSync(promptPath, content, "utf-8");
```

**Ensure directory exists before writing:**
```ts
if (!existsSync(dir)) {
  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });
}
```

**Guard reads:**
```ts
if (!existsSync(filePath)) return null;
try { ... } catch { return null; }
```

If you need a YAML-native store (providers/models use it), look for the actual providerManager/modelManager source — but `idea/ops/store.ts` shows the manual frontmatter-as-string pattern that is used throughout.

